earlier this year the central bank of  russia wanted to ban bitcoin bitcoin  mining and also the use of bitcoin in  any sort of transactions now of course  this is a really really abrasive way to  approach what is a decentralized digital  currency that happens to be getting  global adoption by hundreds of millions  of people around the world well now  they've changed their tune and what  we're seeing is that the russian  government has actually reached a  resolution they don't want to ban it  they simply want to regulate it and so  the russian ministry of finance has  submitted a complete bill to regulate  bitcoin to the cabinet of ministers now  what exactly is in this bill well first  here's the press release that announced  that this was actually getting put  forward what we see is that the ministry  of finance has sent a draft federal law  called on digital currency to the  government of russia what they're  looking for is feedback and ultimately  approval now inside of the bill there's  basically three key components that you  need to know of what russia is trying to  do with bitcoin the first is that they  want to treat crypto as an investment  tool not legal tender they say that  cryptocurrencies may not be used to pay  for goods or services they also want all  sorts of different crypto businesses  whether you're an exchange or an  over-the-counter desk to satisfy certain  criteria to obtain a license and also be  registered with the government and  lastly foreign crypto exchanges must  register as legal entities in russia to  provide services in the country as well  now ultimately this is a little wonky  you're going to actually recognize  bitcoin and cryptocurrencies as  investment tools but not allow them to  be used for the purchase of good or  services that's weird to me  ultimately you can't stop the use of  bitcoin for the purchase of goods and  services bitcoin is a store value it's a  medium of exchange and it is a unit of  account just like any other currency  only in a decentralized way no one can  stop it no one can shut it down and so  ultimately this is a step in the right  direction the russian government is  sitting there saying look this is going  to be a thing we need to get ahead of it  we want to be able to regulate and  they're creating a framework a set of  rules that people will need to follow  but ultimately i think that the citizens  of russia and others around the world  are going to use bitcoin as a medium of  exchange and a unit of account and so  those rules are likely to change  eventually the russian government will  recognize bitcoin not only as an  investment option but also as a medium  of exchange for goods and services and  eventually as a unit of account bitcoin  is inevitable and the russian government  realizes that bitcoin is good for  business so it's great to see them  embracing it creating a set of rules i  just think that they're going to  continue to expand those rules over time
 

